CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS - ALL selected papers must:
- Focus on variants causing rare genetic diseases — including both germline variants and
  post-zygotic mosaic/somatic variants causing non-malignant rare disease phenotypes
- Contain human clinical genetic data with detailed patient phenotypes
- NOT be about cancer-associated somatic mutations, tumor drivers, or acquired
  hematological malignancy mutations
- NOT be about pure cancer predisposition where cancer risk is the PRIMARY manifestation (e.g., BRCA1/BRCA2 breast cancer, Lynch syndrome, Li-Fraumeni, FAP)
  * Exception: Multi-system disorders where cancer is ONE symptom among many (e.g., Beckwith-Wiedemann, Costello syndrome)
- NOT be about CNVs (deletions, duplications, microdeletions, microduplications, chromosomal rearrangements)
- NOT be about gene fusions or fusion transcripts (a chimeric gene formed by joining two genes
  via translocation or other structural rearrangement; e.g., EWSR1-FLI1, EWSR1-NFATC1),
  regardless of somatic or germline status
- NOT be primarily about digenic or oligogenic inheritance (disease requiring variants in
  multiple different genes)
- NOT be primarily about treatment/management/therapy